# Thread `PRRT_kwDOTXdlLc6u-Vsc` — the config SAVE path (`_trajectoryYaml`) is untested

**Test added** (commit `f2d04ae1cb`): `test/cli/cli_config_test.dart`, test *"gh-1745: the save path emits requestBlobs/knobs only when non-default, and they round-trip"* — the same pin the sibling sections carry:

- `CliConfig().toYaml()` writes no `trajectory:` section at all (defaults never written — the file-stays-minimal convention);
- the kill switch saves as `trajectory:\n  requestBlobs: false` (the reviewer's exact assertion, via the real `toYaml()` API);
- non-default knobs save (`requestBlobMaxMb: 10`, `requestBlobTtlDays: 7`) and the derived `requestBlobMaxBytes` never does;
- a full `saveCliConfig` → `loadCliConfig` round-trip re-parses to the same knobs for both the off and tuned shapes.

Test-only change — the save shape was already correct; this pins it against regressions.

# Thread `PRRT_kwDOTXdlLc6u_a_o` — (re-raised) the config SAVE path (`_trajectoryYaml`) is untested

**Test added** (commit `f2d04ae1cb`) — `test/cli/cli_config_test.dart`, *"gh-1745: the save path emits requestBlobs/knobs only when non-default, and they round-trip"*:

- defaults emit nothing (`CliConfig().toYaml()` has no `trajectory:` section);
- the kill switch saves as `trajectory:\n  requestBlobs: false`;
- non-default `requestBlobMaxMb` / `requestBlobTtlDays` save, defaults don't, the derived bytes value never does;
- `saveCliConfig` → `loadCliConfig` round-trips both the off and the tuned shape back to identical knobs.

Test-only — no production change was needed; the asymmetry the thread flagged is closed.
